{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Or has any god tried.</b> Has any deity ever performed wonders <b>to come and take for himself a nation, etc.</b>? All these ה letters are expressions of wonder — therefore they are pointed with a hataf patach: הֲנִהְיָה, הֲנִשְׁמַע, הֲשָׁמַע, הֲנִסָּה." "<b>By trials.</b> Through trials He made His mighty deeds known to them — for instance, ״הִתְפָּאֵר עָלַי״ (Exodus 8): if I am able to do such a thing — this is a trial." "<b>By signs.</b> By signs — to bring them to believe that he is the emissary of the Omnipresent — for instance, ״מַה זֶּה בְיָדֶךָ״ (Exodus 4)." "<b>And by wonders.</b> These are wonders — that He brought upon them wondrous plagues." "<b>And by war.</b> At the sea, as it says, ״כִּי יְהֹוָה נִלְחָם לָהֶם״ (Exodus 14)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:02.850908463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}